The next formula is presented without an assumed named law (1083). [let series]
\begin{equation}q_{1283}\end{equation}

The stored charges satisfy $Q_1+Q_2=Q_3$, without a current statement.

The next formula is presented without an assumed named law (1091). [define as]
\begin{equation}q_{1291}\end{equation}

If the connector were ideal, one might write \[I_a+I_b=I_c\], but leakage is unspecified.

The next formula is presented without an assumed named law (1099). [let series]
\begin{equation}q_{1299}\end{equation}

The quantities are declared as \(I_1=2\,\mathrm{A}\), \(I_2=3\,\mathrm{A}\), and \(I_3=5\,\mathrm{V}\), followed by $I_1+I_2=I_3$.

